; Innermost wins (MAC-HYG-9 M3): a `syntax/for` binding pushed
; inside a template binder of the same spelling answers where the
; template did. Here the template `let` binds `g` to 41 and an
; argument-position `syntax/for` in its body iterates `g` over the
; struct's fields; each for-body `g` resolves to the iteration -
; the inner binder - so the field names `x` and `y` arrive where
; no variable is bound, and the checker refuses both as AX3001.
; Before M3 the ren-first tier rule answered the `let`'s 41, and
; this program lived in tests/selfhost/ as 1003, answering 41 and
; diverging under AXIOM_VERIFY_SCOPES=1 as the scope-equiv gate's
; positive control. The flip moved it here: what the verifier used
; to flag as a parting is now the shipped answer, and a field name
; arriving unbound is the checker's true AX3001, pinned by this
; fixture's golden.
(struct Point
  (x : Int)
  (y : Int))

(macro (probe S) (let ((g 41))
  (S (syntax/for (g (syntax/fields S)) g))))

(:: main Int)
(fn (main)
  (let ((p (probe Point)))
    p.x))
